#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119627 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119816 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c8e217c-252d-529f-a810-84787e2ee886" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Vector is in the Column Space of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "244793f6-41c3-5920-9264-bec32cda9c9c" :question/math-academy-id "e-4807" :question/problem "The matrix $B$ and the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ are given below. \nDetermine if $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Col}(B).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the values of $x_1$ and $x_2,$ where $x_1$ and $x_2$ are the real numbers such that $\\mathbf{b}=x_1\\mathbf{b}_1+x_2\\mathbf{b}_2,$ and $\\mathbf{b}_1,$ $\\mathbf{b}_2$ are the respective columns of $B.$\n\n![](images/a6/a65747aa11107acc9a05df83473ed0208c23818953b16771b608ec4f572dc7ca.svg)" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Col}(B),$ we need to check if the equation $B\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[B \\,|\\, \\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[B\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 15 & -6 & 21 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=7 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get the true statement $0=0.$ So the system is equivalent to the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=7 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $x_2=0.$ Substituting into the first equation gives $x_1=\\dfrac 7 5.$ \n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $B\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent, which implies that $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\textrm{Col}(B).$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $\\mathbf{b}$ as a linear combination of $\\mathbf{b}_1$ and $\\mathbf{b}_2\\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/8a/8a35321d3a29ee86c5af54e23dabd8d3ac93bf7831981507dff3e501796f96a7.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119628 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119817 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "87dc8398-fb5c-564b-a796-db15ff30d72c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Vector Is in the Column Space of a Larger Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "12f222d8-5563-544a-8154-fb1f9406b231" :question/math-academy-id "e-4808" :question/problem "The matrix $C$ and the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ are given below. Determine if $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Col}(C).$ In affirmative case, find the value of $x_1 \\cdot x_2 \\cdot x_3$, where $x_1$, $x_2$, and $x_3$ are real numbers such that $\\mathbf{b}=x_1\\mathbf{c}_1+x_2\\mathbf{c}_3+x_3\\mathbf{c}_3,$ and $\\mathbf{c}_1,$ $\\mathbf{c}_2,$ and $\\mathbf{c}_3$ are the respective columns of $C.$\n\n![](images/02/027332c5a5bdb14913d297e71bc2ac2ae8f846976c1bc3c0c4c569997dcd5b01.svg)" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Col}(C),$ we need to check if the equation $C\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[C \\,|\\, \\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[C\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $x_3=1$. Substituting into the second equation gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{2}+4(1) & =1 \\\\ 3{x}_{2} & =-3 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, from the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =5-{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3} \\\\  & =5-(-1)-4(1) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $C\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent, which implies that $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\textrm{Col}(C).$ \n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $\\mathbf{b}$ as a linear combination of $\\mathbf{c}_1,$ $\\mathbf{c}_2,$ and $\\mathbf{c}_3\\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/4c/4cccd67d5e043d72e0b6949543883e6187d9ef807b7a470146628cbadf7eead7.svg)\n\nFinally, we get $x_1 \\cdot x_2 \\cdot x_3 = 2 \\cdot (-1) \\cdot 1 = -2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119676 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119861 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a557ee8d-51a9-5387-a28c-67ffefed55b4" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of an Unknown Given a Vector That’s in the Column Space of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "b6d52e39-a8a0-5048-80a1-a342a2617e0f" :question/math-academy-id "e-6208" :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by ![](images/fd/fdab914fd2a1013caf1d02dc692df697f4c61f61b3aeba6166b471f3833e7811.svg) Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector ![](images/a8/a8acb2b133143150953e861f13e7b9797756c557800b67ca0334a88d26eb3cc9.svg) belongs to $\\textrm{Col}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Col}(A),$ then the equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A \\,|\\, \\mathbf{b}]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2+k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -32 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2+k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -32 \\\\ 0 & -11 & k-48\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -11 & k-48\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+11{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=10 \\\\ {x}_{2}=4 \\\\ 0=k-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=k-4,$ which means that $k=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408198 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119861 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a557ee8d-51a9-5387-a28c-67ffefed55b4" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of an Unknown Given a Vector That’s in the Column Space of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f479d1d-5d75-5f3c-8153-6a84de5b7ca8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408173} {:answer/id #uuid "be5b0ebc-829b-5a60-838a-1ec9ecacfa60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408184} {:answer/id #uuid "ec6eff0c-554b-5fe5-937d-c0a3c886c493" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408187} {:answer/id #uuid "fb94d986-309a-566f-aca1-f08bcb7d0e0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408189} {:answer/id #uuid "fe6f84ec-14e8-58fa-9f02-c1ec2a769c5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408190}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb94d986-309a-566f-aca1-f08bcb7d0e0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408189} :answer-field/id #uuid "15e1383f-1b6d-5090-8b4e-e602188986c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408191}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5304c962-1643-582f-be3c-68ed826e56d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-110975" :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ k+5\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ then the equation $Ax=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 7 & -2 & k+5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & k+40\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+30\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ {x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 0=k+30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=k+30,$ which means that $k=-30.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408195 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119817 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "87dc8398-fb5c-564b-a796-db15ff30d72c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Vector Is in the Column Space of a Larger Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78645ea0-f8bd-5f81-bf27-fac8caad6e9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(D)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408179} {:answer/id #uuid "7acd09aa-e693-553d-8659-2bccadf0cd4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408180} {:answer/id #uuid "a9c33b38-1f8c-54fe-a1a1-31dc93958a1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408181} {:answer/id #uuid "af5fd598-f27a-56c8-bd28-250a38b55ee9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408182} {:answer/id #uuid "b263cee4-a3ad-5f42-875f-5cc9d7a2c77d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408183}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78645ea0-f8bd-5f81-bf27-fac8caad6e9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(D)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408179} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a398de2-1cab-5e15-93f0-5e8dde00197f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408193}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "06040e86-0928-550a-a9a4-3db2bc9e2e31" :question/math-academy-id "q-111046" :question/problem "The matrix $D$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(D).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}+{x}_{4}$, where ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, ${x}_{3}$, and ${x}_{4}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{d}_{1}+{x}_{2}{d}_{2}+{x}_{3}{d}_{3}+{x}_{4}{d}_{4},$ and ${d}_{1}$, ${d}_{2}$, ${d}_{3}$, and ${d}_{4}$ are respective columns of $D.$\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 6 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 5 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(D),$ we need to check if the equation $Dx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[D\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[D\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 6 & 4 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 5 & -1 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 5 & -1 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}-2{x}_{4}=1 \\\\ 0=6 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}+{x}_{4}=-8 \\\\ {x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}-{x}_{4}=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the  second equation, we get a false statement $0=6.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(D).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317423 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119816 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c8e217c-252d-529f-a810-84787e2ee886" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Vector is in the Column Space of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a344ba4-7e9e-5133-8de4-ea4267e37212" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315176} {:answer/id #uuid "284f1cde-92ac-5c9f-a53e-63c45a513d5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315356} {:answer/id #uuid "45825ac5-30cd-54cc-ad99-cb6dba8de5ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315527} {:answer/id #uuid "866fa2db-6a19-55cd-b98a-1606663103a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(F)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315879} {:answer/id #uuid "a1fac86c-323a-53ee-b319-af0b21358d9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316037}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "284f1cde-92ac-5c9f-a53e-63c45a513d5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315356} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5a252af-653f-5519-a11a-ff0d918098e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316937}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0d0936ed-b5bf-5b20-a019-8454c54094c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-34366" :question/problem "The matrix $F$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(F).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{f}_{1}+{x}_{2}{f}_{2},$ and ${f}_{1},$  ${f}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $F.$\n\n$$\nF=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(F),$ we need to check if the equation $Fx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[F\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[F\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -14\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ 7{x}_{2}=-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$ Substituting into the first equation gives  ${x}_{1}=1.$ \n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $Fx=b$ is consistent, which implies that $b\\in \\text{Col}(F).$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${f}_{1}$ and ${f}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}=1\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{f}_{1}}+(-2)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{f}_{2}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=1\\cdot (-2)=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408196 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119816 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c8e217c-252d-529f-a810-84787e2ee886" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Vector is in the Column Space of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e09706e-9bae-5390-a4c8-454afb7bdba9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408171} {:answer/id #uuid "310c69d2-39ad-5656-a9df-2348bfbcfc3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408172} {:answer/id #uuid "676b432f-8135-5f04-aa24-f35508646c7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408178} {:answer/id #uuid "c34b20ad-6cc0-5427-81db-158ceccf5944" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408185} {:answer/id #uuid "cdc0656a-82ba-50bd-b21a-9c93190c767d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(K)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408186}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdc0656a-82ba-50bd-b21a-9c93190c767d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(K)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408186} :answer-field/id #uuid "529d609f-c755-5038-98fc-5e940ab6a79a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408192}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0a92dafd-51fb-510b-93ec-662d06afe5a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-34503" :question/problem "The matrix $K$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(K).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{k}_{1}+{x}_{2}{k}_{2},$ and ${k}_{1},$ ${k}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $K.$\n\n$$\nK=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(K),$ we need to check if the equation $Kx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[K\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[K\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -18\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-8{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ {x}_{2}=5 \\\\ 0=-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get the false statement $0=-18.$ \n\nTherefore, the system is inconsistent, which implies that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(K).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342192 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119861 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a557ee8d-51a9-5387-a28c-67ffefed55b4" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of an Unknown Given a Vector That’s in the Column Space of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c3a91ab-7081-5091-b24c-88da6615f202" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339241} {:answer/id #uuid "6e125bd2-eb33-5d5b-a7e9-65d561993036" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340109} {:answer/id #uuid "aa0245c9-0ec9-593e-a47c-14041cd652d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340683} {:answer/id #uuid "b283556d-dae4-54a2-bc26-e68126e7df62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340757} {:answer/id #uuid "fa8ff17e-480f-591b-9ddb-16710ee77cc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341351}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa0245c9-0ec9-593e-a47c-14041cd652d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340683} :answer-field/id #uuid "2469311b-dfc4-5722-81d5-ad04c8423a57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341448}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5a3c8192-bc53-5c3d-a7c3-d44d3533846a" :question/math-academy-id "q-74213" :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by $M=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2k+10\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(M).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(M),$ then the equation $Mx=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[M\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[M\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 3 & 2k+10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 3 & 2k+10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 3 & 2k+10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-6){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 15 & 2k+10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-5){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2k-10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ 0=2k-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=2k-10,$ which means that $k=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408197 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119817 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "87dc8398-fb5c-564b-a796-db15ff30d72c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Vector Is in the Column Space of a Larger Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4543a202-3ccc-5eab-b11e-9acd9fffb1d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408174} {:answer/id #uuid "47160327-abda-5117-a3f6-534dafb7314d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408175} {:answer/id #uuid "49158a7c-f7b1-5aa2-a277-f0ac8325fc0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408176} {:answer/id #uuid "56c7eda1-7b63-555c-9f5f-b736c9f51e0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408177} {:answer/id #uuid "fa79a18c-e454-55de-b1b8-442bf38cb930" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408188}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4543a202-3ccc-5eab-b11e-9acd9fffb1d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408174} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb0ebf0b-554c-514b-a72c-5d817e3dd52a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408194}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2009c6af-efbe-5caf-a9f3-bb999b290a0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-74221" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(A).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}$, where ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3},$ and ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and ${a}_{3}$ are the respective columns of $A.$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 10 & -7 \\\\ 3 & -12 & 10\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 11 \\\\ -13\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ we need to check if the equation $Ax=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 10 & -7 & 11 \\\\ 3 & -12 & 10 & -13\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -12 & 10 & -13\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-4 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=3 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting it into the second equation gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}-(-1) & =3 \\\\ 2{x}_{2} & =2 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, from the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =-4+4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} \\\\  & =-4+4(1)-3(-1) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $Ax=b$ is consistent, which implies that $b\\in \\text{Col}(A).$ \n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 11 \\\\ -13\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}=3\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+1\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}+(-1)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=3+1+(-1)=3.$"}]}
